## Additional Terms for Research Use

This repository contains research materials associated with the paper:
"An Empirical Investigation of Large Language Models for Automated Software 
Compliance Testing: Evidence from Web Accessibility"

### Data Attribution
- WCAG test cases are derived from the W3C Accessibility Conformance Testing 
  (ACT) Rules Community Group dataset, which is available under W3C License.
- Original ACT Rules: https://act-rules.github.io/
- W3C Copyright: https://www.w3.org/Consortium/Legal/copyright-documents

### Research Ethics
- This research was conducted following academic ethical standards
- No personal data was collected or processed
- All LLM evaluations used publicly available test cases
- API usage followed respective providers' terms of service

### Citation Requirement
If you use this code, data, or methodology in your research, please cite:

```bibtex
@article{llm_wcag_2025,
  title={An Empirical Investigation of Large Language Models for Automated Software Compliance Testing: Evidence from Web Accessibility},
  author={[Authors]},
  journal={Information and Software Technology},
  year={2025}
}
```

### Commercial Use Disclaimer
While the code is provided under MIT License for research and educational use, 
commercial deployment of LLM-based accessibility testing may require:
- Additional licensing agreements with LLM providers
- Compliance with accessibility testing standards and regulations
- Professional validation of results
- Appropriate human oversight and quality assurance

The authors disclaim any liability for commercial use without proper validation 
and human oversight.